(quality-stats.vox - compile the project's quality numbers from the files
 that already hold them, and write docs/ledger/quality-stats.json.

 The Vox project's public /quality page states how much of LANGUAGE.md
 this fuzzer has actually put on trial. Josj's requirement for that page
 is that every number on it be "compiled from the Vox project and
 Vox-Fuzzer itself, not hardcoded" - a hand-typed figure on a quality
 page is the one kind of number nobody ever re-checks, and it starts
 drifting the day it is typed. So this tool derives each figure from the
 file that owns it, and the site reads one committed artefact.

 CONTRACT. The site reads this file. Its schema was agreed with the site
 master (~/scr/MASTERS-CHANNEL.md, 2026-08-23) - change it there first,
 then here. In particular the site keys off `generated.commit` by name.

 What it reads, and which file owns which number:

   docs/ledger/INDEX.md      the per-section table - one row per
                             LANGUAGE.md section, with its claim count
                             and how many rows are exercised and
                             verified. The totals are the columns
                             summed, never a figure typed anywhere.
   docs/ledger/PROCEDURE.md  the status ladder, for the one-sentence
                             definitions of `exercised` and `verified`
                             that the site prints beside the numbers.
                             INDEX.md's own "How to read the counts"
                             paragraph points here for them, so this
                             follows the pointer rather than paraphrase.
   docs/ledger/probes/       one directory per probe family.
   src/gen_*.vox             the leaf library: every `To 'gen leaf ...`.
   SEEDS.md                  the campaign ledger. docs/ledger/SEEDS.md is
                             tried first, then the repo root, because the
                             ledger has lived in both places.
   docs/findings/            one directory per finding category, each
                             holding numbered finding directories.
   <vox repo>/docs/BUGS_FOUND.md   the defect register: `### N.` entries,
                             classified by their own Status line.
   tests/, <vox repo>/tests/, <vox repo>/tests/compile_fail/

 What it writes: docs/ledger/quality-stats.json, pretty-printed through
 the json library, and a one-line summary on stdout.

 REQUIRED sources - a run stops with exit 2 rather than emit the file if
 any of these is missing or does not parse: INDEX.md's table,
 PROCEDURE.md's two status rows, docs/ledger/probes/, src/gen_*.vox, the
 three test directories, and BUGS_FOUND.md. All of those are numbers the
 page shows as measurements, and a plausible wrong measurement is worse
 than a run that fails loudly: nobody audits a number that looks fine.
 docs/findings/ and SEEDS.md are genuinely optional - a fresh clone that
 has run no campaign has neither - so those emit an empty list or an
 empty count, which is the honest answer, and never a guess.

 Why in Vox: the same reason scripts/invariants.vox and
 scripts/repin-citations.vox are (README, "Why it's written in Vox") - a
 systems tool written in a young language finds bugs in that language by
 existing, and this one is the first vox-fuzz tool to consume a Vox
 shared library, so it exercises the `.lib` path as a side effect of
 doing its job. Nothing here needed a construct the language lacks. The
 two things Vox cannot do alone are listing a directory and running
 `git`, and both go through the same fork/Execute/reap `run shell` that
 invariants.vox and repin-citations.vox already use.

 The json library is consumed as an installed system library, not a
 vendored copy: `see json version "0.1" from "json.lib".` below, with
 the interface found through `--lib-path` - the scripts/quality-stats
 wrapper passes `--lib-path /usr/include/vox`, overridable with
 VOX_LIB_PATH. The `.lib` names its own `.so`, so there is no `-l` and
 no `-L` to get right. The flag is needed at all only because a bare
 `.lib` name does not reach /usr/include/vox on its own - vox #99, open
 as of 2026-08-23. When that closes, the flag comes out of the wrapper
 and this line stays as it is.

 Usage:
   scripts/quality-stats [--out <path>] [--vox-repo <dir>] [--stdout]

   --out       write somewhere other than docs/ledger/quality-stats.json.
   --vox-repo  the sibling vox checkout. Default `../vox`, overridden by
               VOX_REPO, which the wrapper derives from $VOX - a git
               worktree's `../vox` is not the vox repo, so this matters.
   --stdout    print the document instead of writing it.

 Exit codes: 0 wrote the file, 2 a required source was missing or did
 not parse and nothing was written.)

see json version "0.1" from "json.lib".

(---------------------------------------------------------------------
 configuration and state

 Every global lives here, above the functions that read it, because a
 function may only reach a name already declared.
 ---------------------------------------------------------------------)

a text called 'the vox repo' is "../vox".
a text called 'the index path' is "docs/ledger/INDEX.md".
a text called 'the procedure path' is "docs/ledger/PROCEDURE.md".
a text called 'the probes directory' is "docs/ledger/probes".
a text called 'the leaf directory' is "src".
a text called 'the findings directory' is "docs/findings".
a text called 'the tests directory' is "tests".
a text called 'the output path' is "docs/ledger/quality-stats.json".

(The seed ledger has lived in two places. Both are tried, in this order,
 and the first that exists is the one read. A checkout where neither
 exists is not an error - it is a checkout that has run no campaign.)
a text called 'the ledger seed path' is "docs/ledger/SEEDS.md".
a text called 'the root seed path' is "SEEDS.md".

(Opened once, and never closed. `at 2` borrows the descriptor rather than
 naming a path, and `Close` on a borrowed descriptor closes the process's
 stderr for good - after which every later notice, the one that says why
 the run is stopping included, is written into a closed pipe and lost.
 Opening it here also puts it above the functions that write to it.)
open a file for writing called 'the error stream' at 2.

(command line)
a boolean called 'printing to stdout' is false.

(scratch, named by pid so two runs in one checkout cannot collide)
a text called 'the scratch directory' is "".

(Each listing gets its own file, so a later one cannot read an earlier
 one's leftovers if a `find` writes nothing.)
a number called 'listings taken' is 0.

(The defect register's tallies. Globals, because the line that classifies
 one Status line is its own function - an `If` body that ends with a
 nested `If` leaves the outer one open, and a loop written that way never
 reaches its own increment.)
a number called 'register entries found' is 0.
a number called 'register entries fixed' is 0.
a number called 'register entries open' is 0.
a number called 'register entries otherwise' is 0.
a number called 'register entries classified' is 0.

(Left behind by 'lines of' for its own last check, since Vox returns one
 value. This tool only ever reads files, so unlike repin-citations it
 needs no record of whether one ended in a newline.)
a boolean called 'a nul byte was seen' is false.

(---------------------------------------------------------------------
 shell and file helpers - the same shape scripts/invariants.vox and
 scripts/repin-citations.vox use, kept local so this tool depends on
 nothing in src/.
 ---------------------------------------------------------------------)

To 'run shell' with a text called 'the command'.
    a list called 'the shell arguments' is [].
    append "-c" to 'the shell arguments'.
    append 'the command' to 'the shell arguments'.
    a number called 'the child' is fork the process.
    If 'the child' is 0 then, Execute "/bin/sh" with arguments 'the shell arguments', Exit 127.
    a number called 'the reaped' is reap process 'the child'.
    (`reap process` yields the PID; the wait status is a separate
     expression - LANGUAGE.md, "The reaped status".)
    a number called 'the status' is the reaped status.
    a number called 'the terminating signal' is 'the status' bit-and 127.
    If 'the terminating signal' is not 0 then, Return a number, 128 add 'the terminating signal'.
    Return a number, 'the status' divide 256 modulo 256.

(single-quote a value POSIX-style, so a path holding spaces or quotes
 cannot break a command line)
To 'shell quote' with a text called 'the value'.
    a buffer called 'the source bytes' is 'the value'.
    a buffer called 'the quoted bytes' is "'".
    a number called 'the scan position' is 1.
    a number called 'the byte count' is 'the source bytes's size.
    a buffer called 'one byte' is " ".
    While 'the scan position' is less than or equal to 'the byte count',
        a number called 'the current byte' is byte 'the scan position' of 'the source bytes',
        If 'the current byte' is 39 then, append "'\\''" to 'the quoted bytes'.
        If 'the current byte' is not 39 then, Set byte 1 of 'one byte' to 'the current byte', append 'one byte' to 'the quoted bytes'.
        Set 'the scan position' to 'the scan position' add 1.
    append "'" to 'the quoted bytes'.
    a text called 'the result' is 'the quoted bytes' as text.
    Return a text, 'the result'.

(Stop the whole run. Nothing is written on this path, so a failed run
 leaves the previous quality-stats.json exactly as it was rather than
 half-replacing it with a document built from sources that did not read.)
To 'stop with' with a text called 'the reason'.
    Write "quality-stats: {'the reason'}\n" to 'the error stream'.
    If 'the scratch directory' is not "" then, 'run shell' of "rm -rf {'shell quote' of 'the scratch directory'}".
    Exit 2.

(A notice that does not stop the run: an optional source that is absent
 or unreadable. It goes to stderr so it cannot be mistaken for part of
 the summary, and it is said out loud rather than swallowed, because the
 emitted key will be empty and somebody should know why.)
To 'note that' with a text called 'the reason'.
    Write "quality-stats: {'the reason'}\n" to 'the error stream'.

To 'path exists' with a text called 'the path'.
    a number called 'the code' is 'run shell' of "test -e {'shell quote' of 'the path'}".
    Return a boolean, 'the code' is 0.

(A file to a list of its lines, newline stripped. Not a `Read line`
 loop: that cannot tell a blank line from end of file without a separate
 check, and these sources are full of blank lines. One Read fills a
 dynamic buffer with the whole file and the split happens here.)
To 'lines of' with a text called 'the path'.
    a list called 'the result' is [].
    open a file for reading called 'the input file' at 'the path'.
    On error 'stop with' of "cannot read {'the path'}".
    a buffer called 'the file bytes'.
    Read from 'the input file' into 'the file bytes'.
    Close 'the input file'.
    a number called 'the byte count' is 'the file bytes's size.
    Set 'a nul byte was seen' to false.
    a buffer called 'the current line'.
    a buffer called 'one byte' is " ".
    a number called 'the scan position' is 1.
    While 'the scan position' is less than or equal to 'the byte count',
        a number called 'the current byte' is byte 'the scan position' of 'the file bytes',
        If 'the current byte' is 10 then,
            a buffer called 'the line copy' is 'the current line',
            a text called 'the finished line' is 'the line copy' as text,
            append 'the finished line' to 'the result',
            clear 'the current line'.
        If 'the current byte' is not 10 then,
            Set byte 1 of 'one byte' to 'the current byte',
            append 'one byte' to 'the current line'.
        If 'the current byte' is 0 then, Set 'a nul byte was seen' to true.
        Set 'the scan position' to 'the scan position' add 1.
    (A Vox text ends at the first NUL, so a file holding one comes back
     truncated, and a count taken from a truncated file is exactly the
     plausible wrong number this tool exists not to produce.)
    If 'a nul byte was seen' then, 'stop with' of "{'the path'} holds a NUL byte, which a Vox text ends at - refusing to read it rather than counting a truncated file".
    If 'the current line's size is greater than 0 then,
        a buffer called 'the tail copy' is 'the current line',
        a text called 'the tail line' is 'the tail copy' as text,
        append 'the tail line' to 'the result'.
    Return a list, 'the result'.

(The first line of a file, or "" - how a one-line shell result (a short
 sha, a date) is read back, since Vox cannot capture a child's stdout
 directly.)
To 'first line of' with a text called 'the path'.
    a list called 'the read lines' is 'lines of' of 'the path'.
    If 'the read lines's length is 0 then, Return a text, "".
    a text called 'the first' is element 1 of 'the read lines'.
    Return a text, 'the first'.

(Run a command whose output is a listing, and hand back its lines. The
 sort is `LC_ALL=C` so the order is byte order and therefore the same on
 every machine: this file is committed, and a locale-dependent ordering
 would show up as a diff nobody asked for.)
To 'the paths listed by' with a text called 'the find expression' and a text called 'the listing name'.
    a text called 'the listing path' is "{'the scratch directory'}/{'the listing name'}".
    a number called 'the listing code' is 'run shell' of "{'the find expression'} | LC_ALL=C sort > {'shell quote' of 'the listing path'}".
    If 'the listing code' is not 0 then, 'stop with' of "listing failed ({'the listing code'}): {'the find expression'}".
    Return a list, 'lines of' of 'the listing path'.

(---------------------------------------------------------------------
 text scanning. Everything works on a buffer and a 1-based position,
 because that is the shape Vox gives for looking inside text.
 ---------------------------------------------------------------------)

To 'matches at' with a buffer called 'the haystack' and a number called 'the position' and a text called 'the needle'.
    a buffer called 'the needle bytes' is 'the needle'.
    a number called 'the needle length' is 'the needle bytes's size.
    a number called 'the haystack length' is 'the haystack's size.
    If 'the position' is less than 1 then, Return a boolean, false.
    a number called 'the last needed' is {'the position' add 'the needle length'} subtract 1.
    If 'the last needed' is greater than 'the haystack length' then, Return a boolean, false.
    a boolean called 'the answer' is true.
    a number called 'the offset' is 0.
    While 'the offset' is less than 'the needle length' and 'the answer',
        a number called 'the haystack byte' is byte {'the position' add 'the offset'} of 'the haystack',
        a number called 'the needle byte' is byte {'the offset' add 1} of 'the needle bytes',
        If 'the haystack byte' is not 'the needle byte' then, Set 'the answer' to false.
        Set 'the offset' to 'the offset' add 1.
    Return a boolean, 'the answer'.

To 'the line starts with' with a text called 'the line' and a text called 'the opening'.
    a buffer called 'the line bytes' is 'the line'.
    Return a boolean, 'matches at' of 'the line bytes' and 1 and 'the opening'.

(Does a line say a word, whatever case it wrote it in? The register's
 Status lines say "fixed", "**fixed in 0.4.11**" and "Fixed in 0.4.10"
 in about equal numbers, so a case-sensitive test would file a fixed
 defect as unresolved.)
To 'ignoring case, contains' with a text called 'the line' and a text called 'the lowercase needle'.
    a buffer called 'the line bytes' is 'the line'.
    a buffer called 'the lowered' is " ".
    clear 'the lowered'.
    a buffer called 'one byte' is " ".
    a number called 'the byte count' is 'the line bytes's size.
    a number called 'the scan position' is 1.
    While 'the scan position' is less than or equal to 'the byte count',
        a number called 'the current byte' is byte 'the scan position' of 'the line bytes',
        If 'the current byte' is greater than 64 and 'the current byte' is less than 91 then, Set 'the current byte' to 'the current byte' add 32.
        Set byte 1 of 'one byte' to 'the current byte',
        append 'one byte' to 'the lowered',
        Set 'the scan position' to 'the scan position' add 1.
    a boolean called 'the answer' is false.
    Set 'the scan position' to 1.
    While 'the scan position' is less than or equal to 'the byte count' and 'the answer' is false,
        a boolean called 'a match here' is 'matches at' of 'the lowered' and 'the scan position' and 'the lowercase needle',
        If 'a match here' then, Set 'the answer' to true.
        Set 'the scan position' to 'the scan position' add 1.
    Return a boolean, 'the answer'.

(A markdown cell arrives padded, and often wearing the emphasis and code
 markers that make the table readable. The site prints these strings as
 prose, so the markers come off; the words themselves are untouched.)
To 'the plain text of' with a text called 'the cell'.
    a buffer called 'the cell bytes' is 'the cell'.
    a buffer called 'the plain' is " ".
    clear 'the plain'.
    a buffer called 'one byte' is " ".
    a number called 'the byte count' is 'the cell bytes's size.
    a number called 'the scan position' is 1.
    While 'the scan position' is less than or equal to 'the byte count',
        a number called 'the current byte' is byte 'the scan position' of 'the cell bytes',
        a boolean called 'a marker here' is false,
        If 'the current byte' is 96 then, Set 'a marker here' to true.
        If 'matches at' of 'the cell bytes' and 'the scan position' and "**" then, Set 'a marker here' to true, Set 'the scan position' to 'the scan position' add 1.
        If 'a marker here' is false then, Set byte 1 of 'one byte' to 'the current byte', append 'one byte' to 'the plain'.
        Set 'the scan position' to 'the scan position' add 1.
    a number called 'the first kept' is 1.
    a number called 'the last kept' is 'the plain's size.
    While 'the first kept' is less than or equal to 'the last kept' and byte 'the first kept' of 'the plain' is 32,
        Set 'the first kept' to 'the first kept' add 1.
    While 'the last kept' is greater than or equal to 'the first kept' and byte 'the last kept' of 'the plain' is 32,
        Set 'the last kept' to 'the last kept' subtract 1.
    a buffer called 'the trimmed' is " ".
    clear 'the trimmed'.
    a number called 'the copy position' is 'the first kept'.
    While 'the copy position' is less than or equal to 'the last kept',
        Set byte 1 of 'one byte' to byte 'the copy position' of 'the plain',
        append 'one byte' to 'the trimmed',
        Set 'the copy position' to 'the copy position' add 1.
    If 'the trimmed's size is 0 then, Return a text, "".
    a buffer called 'the trimmed copy' is 'the trimmed'.
    a text called 'the answer' is 'the trimmed copy' as text.
    Return a text, 'the answer'.

(The cells of one markdown table row, in order, each already plain and
 trimmed. A row must open and close with a pipe for this to be a row at
 all; anything else answers with no cells, which every caller treats as
 "the table ended here".)
To 'the cells of' with a text called 'the row line'.
    a list called 'the cells' is [].
    a buffer called 'the row bytes' is 'the row line'.
    a number called 'the byte count' is 'the row bytes's size.
    If 'the byte count' is less than 2 then, Return a list, 'the cells'.
    If byte 1 of 'the row bytes' is not 124 then, Return a list, 'the cells'.
    If byte 'the byte count' of 'the row bytes' is not 124 then, Return a list, 'the cells'.
    a buffer called 'the current cell' is " ".
    clear 'the current cell'.
    a buffer called 'one byte' is " ".
    a number called 'the scan position' is 2.
    While 'the scan position' is less than or equal to 'the byte count',
        a number called 'the current byte' is byte 'the scan position' of 'the row bytes',
        If 'the current byte' is 124 then,
            a text called 'the raw cell' is "",
            If 'the current cell's size is greater than 0 then,
                a buffer called 'the cell copy' is 'the current cell',
                Set 'the raw cell' to 'the cell copy' as text.
            a text called 'the finished cell' is 'the plain text of' of 'the raw cell',
            append 'the finished cell' to 'the cells',
            clear 'the current cell'.
        If 'the current byte' is not 124 then,
            Set byte 1 of 'one byte' to 'the current byte',
            append 'one byte' to 'the current cell'.
        Set 'the scan position' to 'the scan position' add 1.
    Return a list, 'the cells'.

(A cell as a whole number, or -1 when it is not one. -1 rather than 0
 because 0 is a real count in most of these columns, and a column that
 failed to parse must never be indistinguishable from a column that
 legitimately says none.)
To 'the number in' with a text called 'the cell'.
    a buffer called 'the cell bytes' is 'the cell'.
    a number called 'the byte count' is 'the cell bytes's size.
    If 'the byte count' is 0 then, Return a number, 0 subtract 1.
    a number called 'the value' is 0.
    a boolean called 'all digits' is true.
    a number called 'the scan position' is 1.
    While 'the scan position' is less than or equal to 'the byte count',
        a number called 'the current byte' is byte 'the scan position' of 'the cell bytes',
        If 'the current byte' is less than 48 then, Set 'all digits' to false.
        If 'the current byte' is greater than 57 then, Set 'all digits' to false.
        If 'all digits' then, Set 'the value' to {'the value' multiply 10} add {'the current byte' subtract 48}.
        Set 'the scan position' to 'the scan position' add 1.
    If 'all digits' is false then, Return a number, 0 subtract 1.
    Return a number, 'the value'.

(Everything after a prefix, as text - how a listing line becomes the name
 of the directory it names.)
To 'the part of' with a text called 'the path' and a text called 'the leading part'.
    a buffer called 'the path bytes' is 'the path'.
    a buffer called 'the prefix bytes' is 'the leading part'.
    a number called 'the byte count' is 'the path bytes's size.
    a number called 'the start' is 'the prefix bytes's size add 1.
    a boolean called 'it leads with that' is 'matches at' of 'the path bytes' and 1 and 'the leading part'.
    If 'it leads with that' is false then, Return a text, 'the path'.
    a buffer called 'the tail' is " ".
    clear 'the tail'.
    a buffer called 'one byte' is " ".
    a number called 'the scan position' is 'the start'.
    While 'the scan position' is less than or equal to 'the byte count',
        Set byte 1 of 'one byte' to byte 'the scan position' of 'the path bytes',
        append 'one byte' to 'the tail',
        Set 'the scan position' to 'the scan position' add 1.
    If 'the tail's size is 0 then, Return a text, "".
    a buffer called 'the tail copy' is 'the tail'.
    a text called 'the answer' is 'the tail copy' as text.
    Return a text, 'the answer'.

(---------------------------------------------------------------------
 the claim ledger - docs/ledger/INDEX.md's table, which is the one
 place the per-section claim counts are written down
 ---------------------------------------------------------------------)

(The row parser reads columns by POSITION, so the positions have to be
 the ones the header names. Without this check a re-ordered table would
 be read silently and wrongly - exercised counts landing under verified
 is exactly the plausible-looking wrong number this tool exists not to
 emit, and a wrong number nobody can see is worse than no file at all.)
To 'insist that column' with a list called 'the header cells' and a number called 'the position' and a text called 'the name'.
    If 'the header cells's length is less than 'the position' then, 'stop with' of "{'the index path'}: the section table's header has {'the header cells's length} columns, too few to hold `{'the name'}` at column {'the position'}".
    a text called 'the column name' is element 'the position' of 'the header cells'.
    If 'the column name' is not 'the name' then, 'stop with' of "{'the index path'}: the section table's column {'the position'} is `{'the column name'}`, expected `{'the name'}` - the columns moved and this tool reads them by position".

To 'the claim row for' with a text called 'the prefix' and a text called 'the ledger' and a text called 'the section' and a number called 'the claims' and a number called 'the exercised' and a number called 'the verified'.
    a map called 'the row' is {}.
    Set 'the row's "prefix" to 'the prefix'.
    Set 'the row's "ledger" to 'the ledger'.
    Set 'the row's "section" to 'the section'.
    Set 'the row's "claims" to 'the claims'.
    Set 'the row's "exercised" to 'the exercised'.
    Set 'the row's "verified" to 'the verified'.
    Return a map, 'the row'.

To 'the claims read from the index'.
    a list called 'the index lines' is 'lines of' of 'the index path'.
    a number called 'the line count' is 'the index lines's length.
    a number called 'the header line' is 0.
    a number called 'the search position' is 1.
    While 'the search position' is less than or equal to 'the line count' and 'the header line' is 0,
        a text called 'one line' is element 'the search position' of 'the index lines',
        If 'the line starts with' of 'one line' and "| prefix | ledger |" then, Set 'the header line' to 'the search position'.
        Set 'the search position' to 'the search position' add 1.
    If 'the header line' is 0 then, 'stop with' of "{'the index path'} has no section table (no row opening `| prefix | ledger |`)".
    a text called 'the header row' is element 'the header line' of 'the index lines'.
    a list called 'the header cells' is 'the cells of' of 'the header row'.
    'insist that column' of 'the header cells' and 1 and "prefix".
    'insist that column' of 'the header cells' and 2 and "ledger".
    'insist that column' of 'the header cells' and 4 and "section".
    'insist that column' of 'the header cells' and 6 and "rows".
    'insist that column' of 'the header cells' and 7 and "exercised".
    'insist that column' of 'the header cells' and 8 and "verified".
    a list called 'the sections' is [].
    a number called 'the total claims' is 0.
    a number called 'the total exercised' is 0.
    a number called 'the total verified' is 0.
    (The header is followed by markdown's dashed separator; the rows run
     from there to the first line that is not a table row.)
    a number called 'the row line' is 'the header line' add 2.
    a boolean called 'still in the table' is true.
    While 'the row line' is less than or equal to 'the line count' and 'still in the table',
        a text called 'one row' is element 'the row line' of 'the index lines',
        a list called 'the cells' is 'the cells of' of 'one row',
        If 'the cells's length is 0 then, Set 'still in the table' to false.
        If 'still in the table' then,
            If 'the cells's length is not 10 then, 'stop with' of "{'the index path'} line {'the row line'}: a section row has {'the cells's length} cells, expected 10 - the table's shape changed and this tool would read the wrong columns".
            a text called 'the prefix' is element 1 of 'the cells',
            a text called 'the ledger' is element 2 of 'the cells',
            a text called 'the section' is element 4 of 'the cells',
            a number called 'the row claims' is 'the number in' of element 6 of 'the cells',
            a number called 'the exercised' is 'the number in' of element 7 of 'the cells',
            a number called 'the verified' is 'the number in' of element 8 of 'the cells',
            If 'the row claims' is less than 0 then, 'stop with' of "{'the index path'} line {'the row line'}: the rows column reads `{element 6 of 'the cells'}`, which is not a count".
            If 'the exercised' is less than 0 then, 'stop with' of "{'the index path'} line {'the row line'}: the exercised column reads `{element 7 of 'the cells'}`, which is not a count".
            If 'the verified' is less than 0 then, 'stop with' of "{'the index path'} line {'the row line'}: the verified column reads `{element 8 of 'the cells'}`, which is not a count".
            a map called 'the section row' is 'the claim row for' of 'the prefix' and 'the ledger' and 'the section' and 'the row claims' and 'the exercised' and 'the verified',
            append 'the section row' to 'the sections',
            Set 'the total claims' to 'the total claims' add 'the row claims',
            Set 'the total exercised' to 'the total exercised' add 'the exercised',
            Set 'the total verified' to 'the total verified' add 'the verified',
            Set 'the row line' to 'the row line' add 1.
        If 'still in the table' is false then, Set 'the row line' to 'the row line' add 1.
    If 'the sections's length is 0 then, 'stop with' of "{'the index path'}: the section table has a header but no rows".
    a map called 'the claim block' is {}.
    Set 'the claim block's "total" to 'the total claims'.
    Set 'the claim block's "exercised" to 'the total exercised'.
    Set 'the claim block's "verified" to 'the total verified'.
    Set 'the claim block's "sections" to 'the sections'.
    Return a map, 'the claim block'.

(---------------------------------------------------------------------
 the definitions the site prints beside the numbers

 "exercised" and "verified" are the whole point of the page, and a
 reader who does not know which is which reads the numbers backwards.
 The sentences come out of PROCEDURE.md's status ladder, which is where
 INDEX.md's own "How to read the counts" paragraph sends a reader for
 them, and that paragraph travels with them because it is what defines
 `rows` - the figure the site calls "claims".
 ---------------------------------------------------------------------)

To 'the status sentence for' with a list called 'the procedure lines' and a text called 'the status'.
    a number called 'the line count' is 'the procedure lines's length.
    a text called 'the sentence' is "".
    a number called 'the scan position' is 1.
    While 'the scan position' is less than or equal to 'the line count' and 'the sentence' is "",
        a text called 'one line' is element 'the scan position' of 'the procedure lines',
        a list called 'the cells' is 'the cells of' of 'one line',
        If 'the cells's length is 2 and element 1 of 'the cells' is 'the status' then, Set 'the sentence' to element 2 of 'the cells'.
        Set 'the scan position' to 'the scan position' add 1.
    Return a text, 'the sentence'.

(The "How to read the counts" paragraph, rejoined into one line. It is
 wrapped across several lines in the file and means nothing broken up.)
To 'the paragraph opening' with a text called 'the opening' and a list called 'the file lines'.
    a number called 'the line count' is 'the file lines's length.
    a number called 'the first line' is 0.
    a number called 'the scan position' is 1.
    While 'the scan position' is less than or equal to 'the line count' and 'the first line' is 0,
        a text called 'one line' is element 'the scan position' of 'the file lines',
        If 'the line starts with' of 'one line' and 'the opening' then, Set 'the first line' to 'the scan position'.
        Set 'the scan position' to 'the scan position' add 1.
    If 'the first line' is 0 then, Return a text, "".
    a buffer called 'the paragraph' is " ".
    clear 'the paragraph'.
    Set 'the scan position' to 'the first line'.
    a boolean called 'still in the paragraph' is true.
    While 'the scan position' is less than or equal to 'the line count' and 'still in the paragraph',
        a text called 'one line' is element 'the scan position' of 'the file lines',
        If 'one line' is "" then, Set 'still in the paragraph' to false.
        If 'still in the paragraph' then,
            If 'the paragraph's size is greater than 0 then, append " " to 'the paragraph'.
            a text called 'the plain line' is 'the plain text of' of 'one line',
            a buffer called 'the line bytes' is 'the plain line',
            append 'the line bytes' to 'the paragraph'.
        Set 'the scan position' to 'the scan position' add 1.
    a buffer called 'the paragraph copy' is 'the paragraph'.
    a text called 'the answer' is 'the paragraph copy' as text.
    Return a text, 'the answer'.

To 'the definitions'.
    a list called 'the procedure lines' is 'lines of' of 'the procedure path'.
    a text called 'the exercised sentence' is 'the status sentence for' of 'the procedure lines' and "exercised".
    a text called 'the verified sentence' is 'the status sentence for' of 'the procedure lines' and "verified".
    If 'the exercised sentence' is "" then, 'stop with' of "{'the procedure path'}: the status ladder has no `exercised` row, so the site would have no definition to print".
    If 'the verified sentence' is "" then, 'stop with' of "{'the procedure path'}: the status ladder has no `verified` row, so the site would have no definition to print".
    a list called 'the index lines' is 'lines of' of 'the index path'.
    a text called 'the counts paragraph' is 'the paragraph opening' of "How to read the counts" and 'the index lines'.
    a map called 'the definition block' is {}.
    Set 'the definition block's "exercised" to 'the exercised sentence'.
    Set 'the definition block's "verified" to 'the verified sentence'.
    Set 'the definition block's "howToReadTheCounts" to 'the counts paragraph'.
    Set 'the definition block's "source" to "{'the procedure path'} (the status ladder) and {'the index path'}".
    Return a map, 'the definition block'.

(---------------------------------------------------------------------
 the probe families and the leaf library
 ---------------------------------------------------------------------)

To 'the probes'.
    If 'path exists' of 'the probes directory' is false then, 'stop with' of "{'the probes directory'} is missing - the probe family count is a measurement the page shows, and zero would be a lie".
    a list called 'the family paths' is 'the paths listed by' of "find {'shell quote' of 'the probes directory'} -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 -type d" and "probe-families.txt".
    a list called 'the leaf paths' is 'the paths listed by' of "find {'shell quote' of 'the leaf directory'} -maxdepth 1 -type f -name 'gen_*.vox'" and "leaf-files.txt".
    If 'the leaf paths's length is 0 then, 'stop with' of "no {'the leaf directory'}/gen_*.vox files - the leaf library is where every generated construct comes from, and an empty list is not a believable answer".
    a number called 'the leaf count' is 0.
    a number called 'the file index' is 1.
    While 'the file index' is less than or equal to 'the leaf paths's length,
        a text called 'one leaf file' is element 'the file index' of 'the leaf paths',
        a list called 'the leaf lines' is 'lines of' of 'one leaf file',
        a number called 'the line index' is 1,
        While 'the line index' is less than or equal to 'the leaf lines's length,
            a text called 'one line' is element 'the line index' of 'the leaf lines',
            If 'the line starts with' of 'one line' and "To 'gen leaf" then, Set 'the leaf count' to 'the leaf count' add 1.
            Set 'the line index' to 'the line index' add 1.
        Set 'the file index' to 'the file index' add 1.
    If 'the leaf count' is 0 then, 'stop with' of "no `To 'gen leaf` definitions found in {'the leaf directory'}/gen_*.vox - either the leaf library moved or its naming changed".
    a map called 'the probe block' is {}.
    Set 'the probe block's "families" to 'the family paths's length.
    Set 'the probe block's "leaves" to 'the leaf count'.
    Set 'the probe block's "leafFiles" to 'the leaf paths'.
    Return a map, 'the probe block'.

(---------------------------------------------------------------------
 the seed ledger - optional, and never invented
 ---------------------------------------------------------------------)

(A count column that does not hold a plain number holds `n/a`, and `n/a`
 is not zero. It becomes null, which is the only honest rendering of a
 sweep that never compiled anything.)
(A leading tilde marks an approximate count — a campaign whose exact
 tally was lost to an interruption. It parses as its number; the row's
 note carries the caveat.)
To 'the count or nothing in' with a text called 'the cell'.
    a text called 'the bare cell' is 'the cell'.
    If 'the line starts with' of 'the cell' and "~" then, Set 'the bare cell' to 'the part of' of 'the cell' and "~".
    a number called 'the count' is 'the number in' of 'the bare cell'.
    If 'the count' is less than 0 then, Return a value, nothing.
    Return a value, 'the count'.

To 'the seed row for' with a list called 'the cells'.
    a map called 'the row' is {}.
    Set 'the row's "date" to element 1 of 'the cells'.
    Set 'the row's "vox" to element 2 of 'the cells'.
    Set 'the row's "voxFuzz" to element 3 of 'the cells'.
    Set 'the row's "seeds" to element 4 of 'the cells'.
    Set 'the row's "budget" to element 5 of 'the cells'.
    Set 'the row's "programs" to 'the count or nothing in' of element 6 of 'the cells'.
    Set 'the row's "compiled" to 'the count or nothing in' of element 7 of 'the cells'.
    Set 'the row's "findings" to 'the count or nothing in' of element 8 of 'the cells'.
    Set 'the row's "note" to element 9 of 'the cells'.
    Return a map, 'the row'.

To 'the seed rows in' with a text called 'the path'.
    a list called 'the rows' is [].
    a list called 'the seed lines' is 'lines of' of 'the path'.
    a number called 'the line count' is 'the seed lines's length.
    a number called 'the header line' is 0.
    a number called 'the search position' is 1.
    While 'the search position' is less than or equal to 'the line count' and 'the header line' is 0,
        a text called 'one line' is element 'the search position' of 'the seed lines',
        If 'the line starts with' of 'one line' and "| Date | vox | vox-fuzz |" then, Set 'the header line' to 'the search position'.
        Set 'the search position' to 'the search position' add 1.
    If 'the header line' is 0 then,
        'note that' of "{'the path'} has no campaign table (no row opening `| Date | vox | vox-fuzz |`) - emitting an empty seed list rather than inventing rows",
        Return a list, 'the rows'.
    a number called 'the row line' is 'the header line' add 2.
    a boolean called 'still in the table' is true.
    While 'the row line' is less than or equal to 'the line count' and 'still in the table',
        a text called 'one row' is element 'the row line' of 'the seed lines',
        a list called 'the cells' is 'the cells of' of 'one row',
        a number called 'the cell count' is 'the cells's length,
        If 'the cell count' is 0 then, Set 'still in the table' to false.
        a boolean called 'the row is malformed' is false,
        If 'still in the table' and 'the cell count' is not 9 then, Set 'the row is malformed' to true.
        If 'the row is malformed' then, 'note that' of "{'the path'} line {'the row line'}: a campaign row has {'the cell count'} cells, expected 9 - emitting an empty seed list rather than half a ledger", Set 'the rows' to [], Set 'still in the table' to false.
        If 'still in the table' then, a map called 'the seed row' is 'the seed row for' of 'the cells', append 'the seed row' to 'the rows'.
        Set 'the row line' to 'the row line' add 1.
    Return a list, 'the rows'.

To 'the seeds'.
    If 'path exists' of 'the ledger seed path' then, Return a list, 'the seed rows in' of 'the ledger seed path'.
    If 'path exists' of 'the root seed path' then, Return a list, 'the seed rows in' of 'the root seed path'.
    'note that' of "no seed ledger at {'the ledger seed path'} or {'the root seed path'} - emitting an empty seed list".
    a list called 'no seed rows' is [].
    Return a list, 'no seed rows'.

(---------------------------------------------------------------------
 the findings - optional, because a clone that has run no campaign has
 none, and none is a real answer
 ---------------------------------------------------------------------)

(Digits in a classification's seed line, as a number: 0 when the line
 names no numeric seed, which is the hand-reduced marker.)
To 'the seed digits of' with a text called 'the seed line'.
    a number called 'the parsed' is 0.
    a text called 'the after' is 'the part of' of 'the seed line' and "seed: ".
    Set 'the parsed' to 'the after' as a number.
    On error Set 'the parsed' to 0.
    Return a number, 'the parsed'.

To 'the findings'.
    a map called 'the finding block' is {}.
    a map called 'by category' is {}.
    If 'path exists' of 'the findings directory' is false then,
        'note that' of "{'the findings directory'} is missing - reporting no findings, which is what a clone that has run no campaign has",
        Set 'the finding block's "curated" to 0,
        Set 'the finding block's "handReduced" to 0,
        Set 'the finding block's "byCategory" to 'by category',
        Return a map, 'the finding block'.
    a list called 'the category paths' is 'the paths listed by' of "find {'shell quote' of 'the findings directory'} -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 -type d" and "finding-categories.txt".
    a list called 'the finding paths' is 'the paths listed by' of "find {'shell quote' of 'the findings directory'} -mindepth 2 -maxdepth 2 -type d" and "findings.txt".
    a number called 'the finding total' is 0.
    a number called 'the category index' is 1.
    While 'the category index' is less than or equal to 'the category paths's length,
        a text called 'one category path' is element 'the category index' of 'the category paths',
        a text called 'the category' is 'the part of' of 'one category path' and "{'the findings directory'}/",
        a number called 'findings in this category' is 0,
        a number called 'the finding index' is 1,
        While 'the finding index' is less than or equal to 'the finding paths's length,
            a text called 'one finding path' is element 'the finding index' of 'the finding paths',
            If 'the line starts with' of 'one finding path' and "{'one category path'}/" then, Set 'findings in this category' to 'findings in this category' add 1.
            Set 'the finding index' to 'the finding index' add 1.
        Set 'by category's "{'the category'}" to 'findings in this category',
        Set 'the finding total' to 'the finding total' add 'findings in this category',
        Set 'the category index' to 'the category index' add 1.
    (A finding whose classification names no numeric seed was reduced by
     hand outside any campaign, so no SEEDS.md row carries it; it joins
     the published total separately. A campaign-seeded finding is already
     in its row's count, so it never adds twice.)
    a number called 'the hand-reduced findings' is 0.
    a number called 'the classification index' is 1.
    While 'the classification index' is less than or equal to 'the finding paths's length,
        a text called 'one classified path' is element 'the classification index' of 'the finding paths',
        a list called 'the classification lines' is 'lines of' of "{'one classified path'}/classification.txt",
        a number called 'the class line index' is 1,
        While 'the class line index' is less than or equal to 'the classification lines's length,
            a text called 'one class line' is element 'the class line index' of 'the classification lines',
            If 'the line starts with' of 'one class line' and "seed:" then,
                a number called 'the parsed seed' is 'the seed digits of' of 'one class line',
                If 'the parsed seed' is 0 then, Set 'the hand-reduced findings' to 'the hand-reduced findings' add 1..
            Set 'the class line index' to 'the class line index' add 1.
        Set 'the classification index' to 'the classification index' add 1.
    Set 'the finding block's "handReduced" to 'the hand-reduced findings'.
    Set 'the finding block's "curated" to 'the finding total'.
    Set 'the finding block's "byCategory" to 'by category'.
    (`curated` and `bugsFiled` are in the agreed schema but no file in
     this repo states either one. An omitted key says "not counted here";
     a zero would say "counted, and there are none". They stay out until
     something owns them.)
    Return a map, 'the finding block'.

(---------------------------------------------------------------------
 the defect register - the vox repo's own docs/BUGS_FOUND.md
 ---------------------------------------------------------------------)

(An entry heading is `### N. title`: the marker, then a digit. The
 register's ordinary section headings are `###` too, so the digit is the
 whole test.)
To 'it opens a register entry' with a text called 'the line'.
    a boolean called 'it is a heading' is 'the line starts with' of 'the line' and "### ".
    If 'it is a heading' is false then, Return a boolean, false.
    a text called 'the numbering' is 'the part of' of 'the line' and "### ".
    a buffer called 'the numbering bytes' is 'the numbering'.
    If 'the numbering bytes's size is 0 then, Return a boolean, false.
    a number called 'the first byte' is byte 1 of 'the numbering bytes'.
    If 'the first byte' is less than 48 then, Return a boolean, false.
    If 'the first byte' is greater than 57 then, Return a boolean, false.
    Return a boolean, true.

(The register's own vocabulary, in the order that decides. An entry that
 says it is fixed is fixed, whatever else the line goes on to say.
 Nothing else is read as a resolution: the entries that say neither are
 documentation corrections and "not a compiler defect" - resolved, but
 never fixed - and counting those as open would put defects on the page
 that do not exist.)
To 'record the status on' with a text called 'the line'.
    Set 'register entries classified' to 'register entries classified' add 1.
    (State-first, the register's convention (vox #11, 2026-08-27): the
     word right after `Status:` names the state, and the rest of the line
     is prose that may mention the other word - `Open - diagnostic fixed
     in v0.4.14` is an OPEN entry. The marker is written four ways:
     `**Status:** fixed`, `**Status:** **fixed**`, `**Status: fixed`,
     and `**Status: **fixed` - so the state word is looked for right
     after `status:` with any run of `*` and spaces between.)
    a boolean called 'it says fixed' is false.
    If 'ignoring case, contains' of 'the line' and "status:** fixed" then, Set 'it says fixed' to true.
    If 'ignoring case, contains' of 'the line' and "status:** **fixed" then, Set 'it says fixed' to true.
    If 'ignoring case, contains' of 'the line' and "status: fixed" then, Set 'it says fixed' to true.
    If 'ignoring case, contains' of 'the line' and "status: **fixed" then, Set 'it says fixed' to true.
    a boolean called 'it says open' is false.
    If 'ignoring case, contains' of 'the line' and "status:** open" then, Set 'it says open' to true.
    If 'ignoring case, contains' of 'the line' and "status:** **open" then, Set 'it says open' to true.
    If 'ignoring case, contains' of 'the line' and "status: open" then, Set 'it says open' to true.
    If 'ignoring case, contains' of 'the line' and "status: **open" then, Set 'it says open' to true.
    If 'it says fixed' then, Set 'register entries fixed' to 'register entries fixed' add 1.
    If 'it says fixed' is false and 'it says open' then, Set 'register entries open' to 'register entries open' add 1.
    If 'it says fixed' is false and 'it says open' is false then, Set 'register entries otherwise' to 'register entries otherwise' add 1.

To 'the register'.
    (Zeroed here rather than trusted to be fresh: the tallies are globals
     so that the classifier can be its own function, and a global that is
     only correct the first time it is read is a trap for whoever calls
     this twice.)
    Set 'register entries found' to 0.
    Set 'register entries fixed' to 0.
    Set 'register entries open' to 0.
    Set 'register entries otherwise' to 0.
    Set 'register entries classified' to 0.
    a text called 'the register path' is "{'the vox repo'}/docs/BUGS_FOUND.md".
    If 'path exists' of 'the register path' is false then, 'stop with' of "{'the register path'} is missing - set VOX_REPO or pass --vox-repo to name the vox checkout".
    a list called 'the register lines' is 'lines of' of 'the register path'.
    a number called 'the line count' is 'the register lines's length.
    a boolean called 'awaiting a status' is false.
    a number called 'the scan position' is 1.
    While 'the scan position' is less than or equal to 'the line count',
        a text called 'one line' is element 'the scan position' of 'the register lines',
        a boolean called 'an entry opens here' is 'it opens a register entry' of 'one line',
        If 'an entry opens here' then, Set 'register entries found' to 'register entries found' add 1, Set 'awaiting a status' to true.
        a boolean called 'a status line' is false,
        If 'awaiting a status' then, Set 'a status line' to 'the line starts with' of 'one line' and "**Status".
        If 'a status line' then, Set 'awaiting a status' to false, 'record the status on' of 'one line'.
        Set 'the scan position' to 'the scan position' add 1.
    If 'register entries found' is 0 then, 'stop with' of "{'the register path'} has no `### N.` entries - the register's heading shape changed".
    If 'register entries classified' is not 'register entries found' then, 'stop with' of "{'the register path'}: {'register entries found'} entries but {'register entries classified'} Status lines - an entry with no status cannot be counted as fixed or open".
    a map called 'the register block' is {}.
    Set 'the register block's "found" to 'register entries found'.
    Set 'the register block's "fixed" to 'register entries fixed'.
    Set 'the register block's "open" to 'register entries open'.
    Set 'the register block's "other" to 'register entries otherwise'.
    Set 'the register block's "source" to "vox docs/BUGS_FOUND.md".
    Return a map, 'the register block'.

(---------------------------------------------------------------------
 the test suites
 ---------------------------------------------------------------------)

To 'the count of vox files in' with a text called 'the directory'.
    If 'path exists' of 'the directory' is false then, 'stop with' of "{'the directory'} is missing - a test count the page shows cannot be guessed".
    Set 'listings taken' to 'listings taken' add 1.
    a text called 'the listing name' is "tests-{'listings taken'}.txt".
    a list called 'the test paths' is 'the paths listed by' of "find {'shell quote' of 'the directory'} -maxdepth 1 -type f -name '*.vox'" and 'the listing name'.
    Return a number, 'the test paths's length.

To 'the tests'.
    a number called 'the fuzzer tests' is 'the count of vox files in' of 'the tests directory'.
    a number called 'the vox run tests' is 'the count of vox files in' of "{'the vox repo'}/tests".
    a number called 'the vox compile fail tests' is 'the count of vox files in' of "{'the vox repo'}/tests/compile_fail".
    a map called 'the vox test block' is {}.
    Set 'the vox test block's "run" to 'the vox run tests'.
    Set 'the vox test block's "compileFail" to 'the vox compile fail tests'.
    a map called 'the test block' is {}.
    Set 'the test block's "voxFuzz" to 'the fuzzer tests'.
    Set 'the test block's "vox" to 'the vox test block'.
    Return a map, 'the test block'.

(---------------------------------------------------------------------
 provenance
 ---------------------------------------------------------------------)

(The vox-fuzz commit recorded is HEAD at the moment of generation, which
 is necessarily the commit BEFORE the one that carries this file - the
 file cannot name the commit that adds it. The site treats a commit that
 is not main's head as "the numbers are from <commit>, <date>", so this
 is exactly the fact it wants. A date and no time: the file is committed,
 and a timestamp would make every regeneration a diff.)
To 'the provenance'.
    a text called 'the answer path' is "{'the scratch directory'}/answer.txt".
    a text called 'the fuzzer commit' is "".
    a number called 'the fuzzer code' is 'run shell' of "git rev-parse --short HEAD > {'shell quote' of 'the answer path'} 2>/dev/null".
    If 'the fuzzer code' is 0 then, Set 'the fuzzer commit' to 'first line of' of 'the answer path'.
    a text called 'the vox commit' is "".
    a number called 'the vox code' is 'run shell' of "git -C {'shell quote' of 'the vox repo'} rev-parse --short HEAD > {'shell quote' of 'the answer path'} 2>/dev/null".
    If 'the vox code' is 0 then, Set 'the vox commit' to 'first line of' of 'the answer path'.
    If 'the vox commit' is "" then, 'stop with' of "cannot read the vox checkout's commit at {'the vox repo'} - the numbers are read against a compiler, and the page names which one".
    a number called 'the date code' is 'run shell' of "date +%Y-%m-%d > {'shell quote' of 'the answer path'}".
    If 'the date code' is not 0 then, 'stop with' of "cannot read today's date ({'the date code'})".
    a text called 'the date' is 'first line of' of 'the answer path'.
    a map called 'the provenance block' is {}.
    Set 'the provenance block's "commit" to 'the fuzzer commit'.
    Set 'the provenance block's "date" to 'the date'.
    Set 'the provenance block's "voxCommit" to 'the vox commit'.
    Set 'the provenance block's "script" to "scripts/quality-stats".
    Return a map, 'the provenance block'.

(Vox has no getpid, so the scratch directory's name is read the way
 src/sandbox.vox and scripts/repin-citations.vox read it: the first field
 of /proc/self/stat. ./vf_* is gitignored and already swept by test.sh,
 which is why every scratch path in this repo lives there.)
To 'self pid'.
    open a file for reading called 'the stat file' at "/proc/self/stat".
    On error Return a number, 0.
    a buffer called 'the stat bytes'.
    Read from 'the stat file' into 'the stat bytes'.
    Close 'the stat file'.
    a buffer called 'the digits' is " ".
    clear 'the digits'.
    a buffer called 'one byte' is " ".
    a number called 'the byte count' is 'the stat bytes's size.
    a number called 'the scan position' is 1.
    a boolean called 'still in digits' is true.
    While 'the scan position' is less than or equal to 'the byte count' and 'still in digits',
        a number called 'the current byte' is byte 'the scan position' of 'the stat bytes',
        If 'the current byte' is less than 48 then, Set 'still in digits' to false.
        If 'the current byte' is greater than 57 then, Set 'still in digits' to false.
        If 'still in digits' then, Set byte 1 of 'one byte' to 'the current byte', append 'one byte' to 'the digits'.
        Set 'the scan position' to 'the scan position' add 1.
    If 'the digits's size is 0 then, Return a number, 0.
    a buffer called 'the digits copy' is 'the digits'.
    a text called 'the pid text' is 'the digits copy' as text.
    Return a number, 'the number in' of 'the pid text'.

(The two ways the document leaves. Both live in functions because a file
 handle opened inside an `If` body belongs to that body, and neither of
 these is reachable except under one.)
To 'write the document' with a buffer called 'the document bytes' and a text called 'the path'.
    open a file for writing called 'the output file' at 'the path'.
    On error 'stop with' of "cannot write {'the path'}".
    Write 'the document bytes' to 'the output file'.
    On error 'stop with' of "write failed on {'the path'}".
    Close 'the output file'.

(Not closed, for the reason the error stream is not: descriptor 1 is
 borrowed from whoever started this program, and closing it would take
 their stdout with it.)
To 'print the document' with a buffer called 'the document bytes'.
    open a file for writing called 'the standard output' at 1.
    On error 'stop with' of "cannot write to standard output".
    Write 'the document bytes' to 'the standard output'.

(---------------------------------------------------------------------
 main
 ---------------------------------------------------------------------)

If the environment variable "VOX_REPO" exists then, Set 'the vox repo' to environment's "VOX_REPO".

a list called 'the arguments' is arguments's all.
a number called 'the argument index' is 1.
While 'the argument index' is less than or equal to 'the arguments's length,
    a text called 'the argument' is element 'the argument index' of 'the arguments',
    a text called 'the value' is "",
    a boolean called 'it takes a value' is false,
    If 'the argument' is "--out" then, Set 'it takes a value' to true.
    If 'the argument' is "--vox-repo" then, Set 'it takes a value' to true.
    If 'it takes a value' then,
        Set 'the argument index' to 'the argument index' add 1,
        If 'the argument index' is greater than 'the arguments's length then,
            Print "quality-stats: {'the argument'} needs a value",
            Exit 2.
        Set 'the value' to element 'the argument index' of 'the arguments'.
    If 'the argument' is "--out" then, Set 'the output path' to 'the value'.
    If 'the argument' is "--vox-repo" then, Set 'the vox repo' to 'the value'.
    If 'the argument' is "--stdout" then, Set 'printing to stdout' to true, Set 'it takes a value' to true.
    If 'it takes a value' is false then,
        Print "quality-stats: unknown argument {'the argument'}",
        Exit 2.
    Set 'the argument index' to 'the argument index' add 1.

a number called 'the pid' is 'self pid'.
Set 'the scratch directory' to "./vf_qstats_{'the pid'}".
a number called 'the scratch made' is 'run shell' of "mkdir -p {'shell quote' of 'the scratch directory'}".
If 'the scratch made' is not 0 then, 'stop with' of "cannot create {'the scratch directory'}".

(Read every source before writing anything. A source that fails takes the
 whole run down with it, and the previous quality-stats.json is still
 whole - which is the point of doing all the reading first.)
a map called 'the definition block' is 'the definitions'.
a map called 'the provenance block' is 'the provenance'.
a map called 'the claim block' is 'the claims read from the index'.
a map called 'the probe block' is 'the probes'.
a list called 'the seed rows' is 'the seeds'.
a map called 'the finding block' is 'the findings'.

(The published total is every finding a campaign recorded: the sum of
 SEEDS.md's findings column. The curated count above is the subset
 written up under docs/findings/.)
a number called 'the campaign finding total' is 0.
a number called 'the seed row index' is 1.
While 'the seed row index' is less than or equal to 'the seed rows's length,
    a map called 'one seed row' is element 'the seed row index' of 'the seed rows',
    a value called 'the row findings' is 'one seed row's "findings",
    If 'the row findings' is a number then, 'the row findings' is a number, Set 'the campaign finding total' to 'the campaign finding total' add 'the row findings'.
    Set 'the seed row index' to 'the seed row index' add 1.

a value called 'the hand-reduced count' is 'the finding block's "handReduced".
If 'the hand-reduced count' is a number then, 'the hand-reduced count' is a number, Set 'the campaign finding total' to 'the campaign finding total' add 'the hand-reduced count'.
Set 'the finding block's "total" to 'the campaign finding total'.
a map called 'the register block' is 'the register'.
a map called 'the test block' is 'the tests'.

a map called 'the document' is {}.
Set 'the document's "definitions" to 'the definition block'.
Set 'the document's "generated" to 'the provenance block'.
Set 'the document's "claims" to 'the claim block'.
Set 'the document's "probes" to 'the probe block'.
Set 'the document's "seeds" to 'the seed rows'.
Set 'the document's "findings" to 'the finding block'.
Set 'the document's "register" to 'the register block'.
Set 'the document's "tests" to 'the test block'.

a text called 'the rendered document' is 'to json with indent' of 'the document' and 2.

(A buffer, never a format string: the document is nothing but `{`, and a
 format string would read every one of them as an interpolation. The
 newline is added because this is a committed text file, and one that
 does not end in a newline becomes a diff on somebody else's commit.)
a buffer called 'the file output' is 'the rendered document'.
append "\n" to 'the file output'.

If 'printing to stdout' then, 'print the document' of 'the file output'.
If 'printing to stdout' is false then, 'write the document' of 'the file output' and 'the output path'.

'run shell' of "rm -rf {'shell quote' of 'the scratch directory'}".

a map called 'the vox test block' is 'the test block's "vox".
a list called 'the section rows' is 'the claim block's "sections".
(Pulled out one per line because a `"key"` cannot be written inside a
 `{...}` interpolation - the quotes would close the string it is in.)
a number called 'the claim total' is 'the claim block's "total".
a number called 'the exercised total' is 'the claim block's "exercised".
a number called 'the verified total' is 'the claim block's "verified".
a number called 'the family count' is 'the probe block's "families".
a number called 'the leaf total' is 'the probe block's "leaves".
a number called 'the register total' is 'the register block's "found".
a number called 'the fixed total' is 'the register block's "fixed".
a number called 'the fuzzer test count' is 'the test block's "voxFuzz".
a number called 'the vox run count' is 'the vox test block's "run".
a number called 'the vox compile fail count' is 'the vox test block's "compileFail".
If 'printing to stdout' is false then,
    Print "quality-stats: {'the claim total'} claims in {'the section rows's length} sections, {'the exercised total'} exercised, {'the verified total'} verified; {'the family count'} probe families, {'the leaf total'} leaves; {'the register total'} register entries, {'the fixed total'} fixed; tests {'the fuzzer test count'} + {'the vox run count'} run + {'the vox compile fail count'} compile-fail -> {'the output path'}".
